div></div>","info":{"doc":"A loop in continuation-passing style, for each `j` from `lo` up to `hi - 1`, followed by the rest\n`k` of the program. The body gets `j`, both its bounds, the continuation `next` and the current\nvariables, and ends by calling `next` on the next variables, which runs the next step, or `k` after\nthe last one. So the variables are arguments of the loop, and a scalar stays unboxed, and a nested\nloop, whose `k` calls the outer `next`, allocates nothing either. A body that doesn't call `next`\nleaves the loop early. `Tail.forIn2`, `Tail.forIn3` and `Tail.forIn4` take two, three and four\nvariables, each its own argument.","docLink":"./ScalarArray/Int16/Program.html#ScalarArray.Int16Array.InPlace.Tail.forIn","kind":"def","line":986,"name":"ScalarArray.Int16Array.InPlace.Tail.forIn","sourceLink":"https://github.com/fgdorais/lean4-scalar-arrays/blob/7ffd513add11df79848981c4efa28480b0e2e483/ScalarArray/Int16/Program.lean#L986-L1001"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./ScalarArray/Int16/Program.html#ScalarArray.Int16Array.InPlace.Tail.forInFrom\"><span class=\"name\">ScalarArray</span>.<span class=\"name\">Int16Array</span>.<span class=\"name\">InPlace</span>.<span class=\"name\">Tail</span>.<span class=\"name\">forInFrom</span></a> </span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">{<span class=\"fn\">n</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Nat\">Nat</a>}</span></span> </span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">{<span class=\"fn\">γ</span> : <a href=\"./foundational_types.html\">Type</a> w}</span></span> </span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">{<span class=\"fn\">β</span> : <a href=\"./foundational_types.html\">Type</a> v}</span></span> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">lo </span><span class=\"fn\">hi </span><spa