ml#ScalarArray.Int16Array.InPlace.Tail.done\"><span class=\"name\">ScalarArray</span>.<span class=\"name\">Int16Array</span>.<span class=\"name\">InPlace</span>.<span class=\"name\">Tail</span>.<span class=\"name\">done</span></a> </span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">{<span class=\"fn\">n</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Nat\">Nat</a>}</span></span> </span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">{<span class=\"fn\">α</span> : <a href=\"./foundational_types.html\">Type</a> u}</span></span> </span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">{<span class=\"fn\">γ</span> : <a href=\"./foundational_types.html\">Type</a> w}</span></span> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">x</span> : <span class=\"fn\">α</span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">k</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">α</span> → <span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">a</span> : <a href=\"./ScalarArray/Int16/Basic.html#ScalarArray.Int16Array\">Int16Array</a>) → <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">a</span>.<a href=\"./ScalarArray/Int16/Basic.html#ScalarArray.Int16Array.size\">size</a></span> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Eq\">=</a> <span class=\"fn\">n</span> → <span class=\"fn\">γ</span></span></span></span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./ScalarArray/Int16/Program.html#ScalarArray.Int16Array.InPlace.Tail\">Tail</a> <span class=\"fn\">n</span> <span class=\"fn\">γ</span></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Ends the program with the result `x`: hands `x`, the array and its size to `k`.","docLink":"./ScalarArray/Int16/Program.html#ScalarArray.Int16Array.InPlace.Tail.done","kind":"def","line":890,"name":"ScalarArray.Int16Array.InPlace.Tail.done","sourceLink":"https://github.com/fgdorais/lean4-scalar-arrays/blob/7ffd513add11df79848981c4efa28480b0e2e483/ScalarArray/Int16/Program.lean#L890-L893"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">structure</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./ScalarArray/Int16/Program.html#ScalarArray.Int16Array.InPlace.Tail\"><span class=\"name\">ScalarArray</span>.<span class=\"name\">Int16Array</span>.<span class=\"name\">InPlace</span>.<span class=\"name\">Tail</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">n</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Nat\">Nat</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">γ</span> : <a href=\"./foundational_types.html\">Type</a> u)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./foundational_types.html\">Type</a> u</div></div>","info":{"doc":"A tail program on arrays of size `n`, which returns a `γ`: an in-place program that ends by handing\nthe new array to a continuation, instead of returning it with a result. The continuation runs where\nthe program ends, inside its last loop if it ends with one, so the program's last values reach it\nunboxed, and no result pair is built. A tail program is built from in-place programs with\n`Tail.bind`, `Tail.readThen`, `Tail.ite`, `Tail.dite`, the loops `Tail.forInBind`,\n`Tail.forIn2Bind`, `Tail.forInRevBind` and `Tail.forInRev2Bind`, and ends with `Tail.done x k`.\nIt runs with `Tail.run` or `runInPlaceThen`, and `inplace a do … then k` writes one.","docLink":"./ScalarArray/Int16/Program.html#ScalarArray.Int16Array.InPlace.Tail","kind":"structure","line":873,"name":"ScalarArray.Int16Array.InPlace.Tail","sourceLink":"https://github.com/fgdorais/lean4-scalar-arrays/blob/7ffd513add11df79848981c4efa28480b0e2e483/ScalarArray/Int16/Program.lean#L873-L884"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">theorem</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./ScalarArray/Int16/Program.html#ScalarArray.